### **Monitoring & Prevention Framework**

#### **Essential Metrics to Track**

**Training Health:**
- Loss (train/val), per-component if multi-objective
- Gradient norms (global, per-layer, max/mean/std)
- Learning rate schedule
- Parameter norms and update magnitudes
- Throughput (samples/sec, tokens/sec)
- Memory usage

**Model Health:**
- Activation statistics (mean, std, % dead)
- Attention entropy distribution
- Embedding space metrics (isotropy, nearest-neighbor)
- Layer-wise gradient flow

**Numerical Health:**
- NaN/Inf counters
- Overflow/underflow events
- Mixed precision loss scale

**System Health:**
- GPU utilization
- Memory fragmentation
- I/O bottlenecks
- Communication overhead (distributed)

#### **Alerting Thresholds**

Configure alerts for anomaly detection:
- Loss spikes > 2x rolling average
- Gradient norm > 10x baseline
- Any NaN/Inf occurrence
- GPU utilization < 50%
- Memory approaching limit

#### **Checkpoint Strategy for Diagnostics**

- Save checkpoints at regular intervals for forensic analysis
- Include optimizer state for full reproducibility
- Log key metrics at each checkpoint for correlation
- Enable checkpoint rollback for recovery from divergence

